        "chapter": 1,
        "verse": 3
      },
      {
        "text": "And behold, ye shall take the plates of Nephi unto yourself, and the remainder shall ye leave in the place where they are; and ye shall engrave on the plates of Nephi all the things that ye have observed concerning this people.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 30,
            "end": 45,
            "text": "W of M 1:1 (1, 11); 3 Ne. 5:10 (9–12); Morm. 2:17 (17–18); 8:5 (1, 4–5, 14)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 4,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "The Book of Mormon 1:4",
        "book": "The Book of Mormon",
        "chapter": 1,
        "verse": 4
      },
      {
        "text": "And I, Mormon, being a descendant of Nephi, (and my father’s name was Mormon) I remembered the things which Ammaron commanded me.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 37,
            "end": 42,
            "text": "3 Ne. 5:20 (12, 20)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 5,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "The Book of Mormon 1:5",
        "book": "The Book of Mormon",
        "chapter": 1,
        "verse": 5
      },
      {
        "text": "And it came to pass that I, being eleven years old, was carried by my father into the land southward, even to the land of Zarahemla.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 6,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "The Book of Mormon 1:6",
        "book": "The Book of Mormon",
        "chapter": 1,
        "verse": 6
      },
      {
        "text": "The whole face of the land had become covered with buildings, and the people were as numerous almost, as it were the sand of the sea.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 7,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "The Book of Mormon 1:7",
        "book": "The Book of Mormon",
        "chapter": 1,
        "verse": 7
      },
      {
        "text": "And it came to pass in this year there began to be a war between the Nephites, who consisted of the Nephites and the Jacobites and the Josephites and the Zoramites; and this war was between the Nephites, and the Lamanites and the Lemuelites and the Ishmaelites.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 69,
            "end": 77,
            "text": "4 Ne. 1:36."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 8,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "4 Ne. 1:36.",
            "prettyString": "4 Nephi 1:36",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "scripture",
                "book": "4nephi",
                "chapters": [
                  {
                    "start": 1,
                    "end": 1,
                    "verses": [
                      {
                        "start": 36,
                        "end": 36
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "The Book of Mormon 1:8",
        "book": "The Book of Mormon",
        "chapter": 1,
        "verse": 8
      },
      {
        "text": "Now the Lamanites and the Lemuelites and the Ishmaelites were called Lamanites, and the two parties were Nephites and Lamanites.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 8,
            "end": 17,
            "text": "4 Ne. 1:20."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 9,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "4 Ne. 1:20.",
            "prettyString": "4 Nephi 1:20",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "scripture",
                "book": "4nephi",
                "chapters": [
                  {
                    "start": 1,
                    "end": 1,
                    "verses": [
                      {
                        "start": 20,
                        "end": 20
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "The Book of Mormon 1:9",
        "book": "The Book of Mormon",
        "chapter": 1,
        "verse": 9
      },
      {
        "text": "And it came to pass that the war began to be among them in the borders of Zarahemla, by the waters of Sidon.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 10,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "The Book of Mormon 1:10",
        "book": "The Book of Mormon",
        "chapter": 1,
        "verse": 10
      },
      {
        "text": "And it came to pass that the Nephites had gathered together a great number of men, even to exceed the number of thirty thousand. And it came to pass that they did have in this same year a number of battles, in which the Nephites did beat the Lamanites and did slay many of them.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 198,
            "end": 205,
            "text": "2 Ne. 1:12; Morm. 4:1 (1–23)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 11,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "The Book of Mormon 1:11",
        "book": "The Book of Mormon",
        "chapter": 1,
        "verse": 11
      },
      {
        "text": "And it came to pass that the Lamanites withdrew their design, and there was peace settled in the land; and peace did remain for the space of about four years, that there was no bloodshed.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 12,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "The Book of Mormon 1:12",
        "book": "The Book of Mormon",
        "chapter": 1,
        "verse": 12
      },
      {
        "text": "But wickedness did prevail upon the face of the whole land, insomuch that the Lord did take away his beloved disciples, and the work of miracles and of healing did cease because of the iniquity of the people.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 101,
            "end": 108,
            "text": "3 Ne. 28:12 (2, 12)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 13,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "The Book of Mormon 1:13",
        "book": "The Book of Mormon",
        "chapter": 1,
        "verse": 13
      },
      {
        "text": "And there were no gifts from the Lord, and the Holy Ghost did not come upon any, because of their wickedness and unbelief.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 18,
            "end": 23,
            "text": "1 Sam. 3:1."
          },
          {
            "start": 47,
            "end": 57,
            "text": "TG Holy Ghost, Loss of."
          },
